    "result": "Excellent! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Found and Fixed\n\n**Issue 1: Missing named export in `src/finetune/index.js`**\n- The test tried to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only in the default export\n- Fixed by adding a named export statement for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n**Issue 2: Incorrect parameter passing in `src/eval/index.js`**\n- The `runEvaluations` function always passed both outputs and references to all metrics\n- The `toxicityMetric` function only needs outputs (and optional bannedTerms), not references\n- When called with references as the second parameter, it incorrectly interpreted them as banned terms, causing false positives\n- Fixed by using `function.length` to check if a metric requires 2+ parameters before passing references\n\n## Commands Run and Results\n\n```bash\npnpm --filter frai-core build\n# Output: No build step needed - ES modules\n\npnpm --filter frai-core test\n# Result: \u2713 8 test files passed\n#         \u2713 28 tests passed\n```\n\nAll existing public exports remain working, and the test suite now passes completely.",
